########## Exercise 11.3.8(b) as stated: replace j by m = i - 2j, keep i ##########

==== (a) m = i - 2j, order m,i (j determined) ====
  constraints with the equality m = ... added as two rows  (vars: m i j )
    i - 1 >= 0
    -i + 29 >= 0
    -i + j - 2 >= 0
    -i - j + 39 >= 0
    m - i + 2*j >= 0
    -m + i - 2*j >= 0
  generated code:
for (m = -75; m <= -5; m++)
  for (i = 1; i <= min(-m - 4, floor_div(m + 78, 3)); i++)
    for (j = ceil_div(-m + i, 2); j <= floor_div(-m + i, 2); j++)
      X[i][j] = 0;
  verify (a) m = i - 2j, order m,i (j determined): 342 iterations, IDENTICAL point set to brute force (no duplicates)
  first iterations in generated order: [1,38] [1,37] [2,37] [1,36] [2,36] [1,35] [3,36] [2,35] [1,34] [3,35] ...

==== (b) m = i - 2j, order m,i (j determined) ====
